  "REAL Dockstore response, EXCERPT. Fetched 2026-10-15 with:",
  "  curl -sS 'https://dockstore.org/api/workflows/path/workflow/github.com%2Fbroadinstitute%2Fgatk-sv%2FGenotypeBatch/published?include=versions'",
  "which answers HTTP 200 UNAUTHENTICATED -- no token, no cookie. This is the route GitHub issue #3 named and the one",
  "this repo's own docs claimed was closed to anonymous readers (401). That claim was WRONG and is corrected in",
  "checks/version_resolves.py's docstring and docs/static-checks.md: what answers 401 is the SAME PATH WITHOUT",
  "`/published`; what answers 200 with a commitID on EVERY version row is this route. Getting the two backwards is",
  "how a stale-WDL check ended up documented as impossible to run.",
  "",
  "EXCERPT: 4 of the entry's 28 version rows are kept -- the three the field case needs (mw_genotype_scale, its",
  "_terra sidecar, main) plus one unrelated real row so this is not a single-purpose mock. The rest are dropped",
  "because a full listing is a list of other people's branch names, the standing policy for committed captures (see",
  "README.md beside this file); `versions_dropped: 24` says so in data rather than prose. Metadata blocks with no",
  "bearing on the check are trimmed from the entry and the rows alike.",
  "",
  "THE DECOYS ARE LOAD-BEARING -- DO NOT 'TIDY' THEM. On this body `workflow_path` is the DESCRIPTOR FILE inside the",
  "repo (/Dockstore.cwl) and `path` is the repo (github.com/broadinstitute/gatk-sv). Both contain a `/`, so both",
  "satisfy a generic 'is this an entry path?' test; reading the entry from either files all versions under a .cwl",
  "filename and then answers ABSENT for the entry actually asked about -- a wrong answer that looks like an answer.",
  "The entry comes from `full_workflow_path`. `id` is the numeric DB id, the third decoy, already refused by",
  "`_path_of` for exactly that reason."
